@startuml 05-list-snippets
title Listar snippets accesibles con filtros y orden (US #5)
autonumber

actor "Usuario" as user
participant "UI" as ui
participant "nginx" as nginx
participant "Snippet Service" as snippet
participant "Permission Service" as perm
database "Permission DB" as pdb
database "Snippet DB" as sdb

user -> ui : elige relación, filtros y orden
ui -> nginx : GET /api/snippets?relation=shared&name=hol&valid=true\n&sort=name,asc&page=0&size=20 (JWT)
nginx -> snippet : GET /snippets?...
snippet -> snippet : valida JWT y obtiene userId

snippet -> perm : GET /permissions/snippets?userId=&relation=shared
perm -> pdb : SELECT snippet_id WHERE user_id = ? AND role = READ
pdb --> perm : ids
perm --> snippet : [snippetIds]

snippet -> sdb : SELECT ... WHERE id IN (snippetIds)\nAND name ILIKE '%hol%' AND lint_status = 'VALID'\nORDER BY name ASC LIMIT 20 OFFSET 0
sdb --> snippet : página de snippets + total

snippet --> nginx : 200 { content: [...], page, size, total }
nginx --> ui : 200
ui --> user : muestra la lista con su validez

note right of perm
  relation:
  owned  → role = OWNER
  shared → role = READ
  all    → ambos
end note

note over snippet, sdb
  El contenido no se lee de Blob Storage para listar:
  la lista solo usa la metadata de la base.
end note

@enduml
